[ ] archive charter moves every charter-local completed history file $Archiving graph-views moved graph-views.completed.actions but left next.completed.actions behind under charters/graph-views, keeping a ghost active directory. The leftover was moved manually to archive/graph-views for this cleanup. Fix archive discovery so all charter-local supporting files move atomically, including alternate *.completed.actions histories.$ !2 +bug #019f7457-51fc-7e02-90bf-d2cdb11f2964
[ ] make fresh init produce a resolvable root charter and routable plan directories $Dogfood e2e in /tmp/clearhead-dogfood.wdSBZS: init then add charter --alias dogfood emits an implicit parent equal to the workspace display name, which doctor reports as unresolvable. add plan --charter dogfood then writes under plans/<workspace>-dogfood; loader invents a charterless Plan owner, and sync calendar fails: charter carries plans but has no actions_file to stamp into. Fresh-workspace add/action/archive and graph otherwise work. Add an acceptance test covering init -> add charter -> add recurring plan -> sync calendar.$ !1 +bug #019faff7-0066-7ea1-b717-040802e75ebf
[ ] honor read plans output formats and handle closed stdout without panicking $Dogfood against the real user workspace: clearhead read plans --format ids, --format json-ld, and --format json all render the same table, contrary to help and unlike read actions. Separately, piping read charters/actions into head can panic at stdio.rs with Broken pipe instead of exiting cleanly. Add CLI acceptance coverage for explicit formats and early consumer close.$ !2 +bug #019faff8-1580-77c2-b8d6-94967efdb792
